13lu|n|A kind of frock for children. ; See Jamb. ; A mass of people or objects crowded together; also, the pressure from a crowd; a crush; as, a jam in a street; a jam of logs in a river. ; An injury caused by jamming. ; A preserve of fruit boiled with sugar and water; as, raspberry jam; currant jam; grape jam.	n:rpw,36,6~rpw,36,6	N:pad,56,3~pad,56,3
